.TH "SPGEN-SCHEMA-TYPESCRIPT" "1" "" "spgen 0.1.0" ""
.SH NAME
spgen\-schema\-typescript \- Generates the WarpDrive resource schema and the citizen's registrations
.SH SYNOPSIS
pnpm spgen schema <read\-model>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generates the WarpDrive resource schema and the citizen's registrations
.SS "Generated files"
.IP \[bu] 2
apps/<subdomain>/src/<composite>/schemas/<constituent>.ts (resource schema with defaults)
.IP \[bu] 2
apps/<subdomain>/src/<composite>/index.ts (export registration here)
.IP \[bu] 2
apps/<subdomain>/src/config.ts (citizen registration in config)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-subdomain\fR \fI<SUBDOMAIN>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-composite\fR \fI<COMPOSITE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-constituent\fR \fI<CONSTITUENT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
model root, default docs/domain\-model (relative to \-\-root)
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR
repo root, default inferred from the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
report the drift, write nothing
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
FE: rewrite present generated units in place
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIREAD\-MODEL\fR>
the element: esdm: reference, *.esdm.yaml, kind.name, or bare name
.SH "SEE ALSO"
spgen(1)
suites: domain\-objects, feature
